# Architecture

Stack: Flutter (Impeller) mobile client, FastAPI backend, PostgreSQL. No Unity/Godot. No Firebase.

## World-agnostic engine

Mechanics (steps, armaments, checkpoints, streaks, affliction stubs) deal only in **generic keys and numbers**. A world is a content bundle (terminology + lore + art theme) layered on top. Never hardcode fictional names in engine, API, or widgets.

Resolve every user-facing mythos string through the terminology table at render time:

```dart
// BAD
Text('Rest at a Held Breath');

// GOOD
Text('Rest at ${terms.resolve(TermKey.checkpointName)}');
```

## Layers

- Backend: `api/` (thin routers) → `domain/` (pure logic) → `infra/` / `models/` (DB). No business logic in routers.
- Mobile: `presentation/` → `domain/` → `data/`. No HTTP or SQL in widgets.
- Content lives in `content/worlds/` as YAML; seed into Postgres. Engine never imports YAML directly for runtime decisions if the DB is the source of truth.

## IP

Do not use, even as placeholders in code or comments: Tarnished, Scarlet Rot, Site of Grace, Bloodstain, or any FromSoftware proper noun. Generic keys: `checkpoint`, `deathMarker`, `affliction`, `summons`.
